    "title": "Acceptance Wording Guard",
    "statement": "Acceptance and qualification checks must not depend on generated natural-language wording. Two owner qualification runs have been lost to this defect class (ADR-0051 addendum 2, 2026-09-04; ADR-0051 addendum 4, 2026-09-05, where `speech_head -like \"Efendim, son ara*\"` failed a system that was working because the briefing had been made shorter and better worded the same day). The recorded decision -- generated wording is never acceptance evidence; paraphrasing is free, an unsupported claim is not -- is enforced by nothing. Build a read-only checker that reports acceptance assertions resting on generated prose, with a low-false-positive, subject-driven design and a reasoned allow-list, and report the shape of each match rather than the matched text.",
